  "generated_text": "To find the average (mean) of all 5-digit numbers that can be formed using the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7, 8\\) exactly once, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the total number of 5-digit numbers:**\n   Each digit can be placed in any of the 5 positions. Since the digits are distinct, the total number of permutations is \\(5!\\):\n   \\[\n   5! = 5 \\times 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 120\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the contribution of each digit to each place value:**\n   Each digit will appear in each place (units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands) an equal number of times. To find this number, we divide the total permutations by the number of digits in each place:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{120}{5} = 24\n   \\]\n   So, each digit will appear in each place value 24 times.\n\n3. **Calculate the sum of all the 5-digit numbers:**\n   To find the sum, we need to consider the contribution of each digit in each place value. The sum of the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7, 8\\) is:\n   \\[\n   1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8 = 24\n   \\]\n   Each digit will appear in each place 24 times. Therefore, the contribution of each digit to the sum in each place value is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Contribution of a digit in one place} = \\text{digit} \\times 24 \\times \\text{place value}\n   \\]\n   For example, the contribution of the digit 1 in the units place is:\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 24 \\times 1 = 24\n   \\]\n   Similarly, the contributions of the digits 3, 5, 7, and 8 in the units place are:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 24 \\times 1 = 72, \\quad 5 \\times 24 \\times 1 = 120, \\quad 7 \\times 24 \\times 1 = 168, \\quad 8 \\times 24 \\times 1 = 192\n   \\]\n\n   Summing these contributions for all place values (units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total sum} = (1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8) \\times 24 \\times (1 + 10 + 100 + 1000 + 10000)\n   \\]\n   Simplifying inside the parentheses:\n   \\[\n   1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8 = 24\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1 + 10 + 100 + 1000 + 10000 = 11111\n   \\]\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total sum} = 24 \\times 24 \\times 11111 = 6999936\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the average (mean) of the 5-digit numbers:**\n   The average is the total sum divided by the total number of numbers:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Average} = \\frac{6999936}{120}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6999936}{120} = 58332.8\n   \\]\n\nThus, the average (mean) of all 5-digit numbers that can be formed using the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7, 8\\) exactly once is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{58332.8}\n\\]",
